---
source: crates/squawk_linter/src/rules/ban_truncate_cascade.rs
expression: "lint_errors(sql, Rule::BanTruncateCascade)"
---
warning[ban-truncate-cascade]: `cascade` recursively truncates every table with a foreign key to the truncated tables
  ╭▸ 
2 │         truncate a, b, c cascade;
  │                          ━━━━━━━
  │
  ├ note: with foreign keys set up as `a <- b <- c`, truncating `a` also truncates `b` and `c`
  ╰ help: remove the `cascade` and list exactly which tables to truncate
